        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Build a keyboard: one polyphonic synth and three ways to play it, all at once. Press Space and a demo phrase plays.\n\nPlay along: press Ctrl+K (or the keyboard button in the transport bar) to turn on Play keys. The middle row of letters, A S D F G H J K L, plays the white keys up from middle C and W E T Y U O P the black keys; Z and X shift an octave down and up. Or click the on-screen keyboard's keys. Hold several keys for chords, and turn Demo off to play on your own.\n\nCtrl+Tab shows the Play panel, the keyboard and knobs without the wires; F11 plays it full screen, with Play keys on."
        },
        "ui": {
