      {
        "id": "9",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Keyboard In turns the computer keys into MIDI notes, and Keyboard is a piano you click; Velocity sets how hard both of them play, and Octave shifts the on-screen keys. The Demo phrase is a MIDI Pattern: select it to see its notes in the Node tab's piano roll. The Demo gate, a Switch set to carry MIDI, passes it while Demo is on.\n\nAn input takes one wire, so a Merge joins all three into Notes. A note played from two of them at once sounds once and ends when both let go, and turning Demo off lets go of the demo's notes, so nothing hangs."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            450.0
          ],
          "size": [
            736.0,
            136.0
          ]
        }
